<title>BANGLADESH: Three Bangladeshis companies offer IPOs.</title>
<headline>Three Bangladeshis companies offer IPOs.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Bangladeshi companies go public this month with initial public offering (IPOs) totalling 135 million taka, market sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The companies are Uttara Finance and Investment Limited, Samorita Hospital Limited and Rose Heaven Ball Pen Limited. Uttara Finance and Investment Limited (UFIL) opened for subscription on July 6 and will close on July 15. It offered 400,000 ordinary shares of 100 taka each to the public.</p>
</text>
